# Code Modularity & File Structure

Build the product as small, composable, reusable units — never one growing
file that does everything. This is about *file/module* decomposition;
function-level shape lives in `code-clarity-and-comments.mdc`, OOP shape in
`oop-and-domain-modeling.mdc`, and cross-package boundaries in `architecture.mdc`.

## One concern per file

- A file exports **one cohesive thing** (a component + its tiny local helpers,
  one router, one service, one hook). If a file needs the word "and" to
  describe it, split it.
- **File size is a smell signal, not a hard limit:** past ~200–300 lines, stop
  and ask "what distinct responsibility can move out?" Long files are where
  ownership checks, edge cases, and dead code hide.
- Never create catch-all `utils.ts` / `helpers.ts` / `misc.ts` buckets. Name
  the module for the concern (`marketplace-geo.ts`, `ledger-display.ts`), as
  the codebase already does.

## Extract for reuse (the "rule of two/three")

- Inline the first time. On the **second** copy, extract a named, typed,
  tested unit; don't wait for the third. Avoid the opposite failure too — no
  speculative abstraction for a single caller.
- Reused pure logic → a function in the right package (`packages/domain/*` for
  business rules, a small shared lib package for generic helpers).
- Reused server/composition logic (DTO mappers, query shapers) → a `lib/`
  helper imported by the routers that need it, not copy-pasted per router.
- Reused presentational UI → `packages/ui` (no data fetching, no business
  logic). Feature-specific UI → colocate under `apps/web/components/<area>/`.

## Where shared code belongs (follow `architecture.mdc`)

| Kind of code | Home |
|---|---|
| Shapes/enums shared across packages | `packages/types` (Zod + `z.infer`) |
| Pure business rules | `packages/domain/*` |
| tRPC routers / composition | `packages/api-client` (one file per area) |
| Reusable presentational components | `packages/ui` |
| Feature/page-local components | `apps/web/components/<area>/` |
| Cross-feature web helpers | `apps/web/lib/<concern>.ts` |

Do not solve "shared between two routes" by importing from another route's
folder — lift it to the appropriate shared location instead.

## Components

- Decompose a page into **named section components**; a page/component that
  renders many independent sections inline is a god component — extract each
  section (the marketplace profile already does this:
  `society-location-section.tsx`, `society-payment-plans.tsx`, etc.).
- Default to Server Components; push `"use client"` to the smallest
  interactive leaf (`nextjs-app-router.mdc`).
- Reusable client logic → a custom hook in a `hooks/` file, not duplicated
  effect/state across components.
- Props are a single typed object; keep positional params ≤3
  (`code-clarity-and-comments.mdc`).

## Public API & imports

- Each package's public surface is its `src/index.ts` **barrel**; import across
  packages from the barrel, never deep-import an internal file
  (`@sectoria/types`, not `@sectoria/types/src/society.js` internals).
- Within a package, prefer explicit `.js` specifiers per the repo's NodeNext
  ESM convention (see existing files).

## Services

- A service is a cohesive set of functions over one concern, exposed through
  `packages/api-client`. It composes domain + persistence; it does not
  reimplement business rules inline (`api-trpc.mdc`,
  `oop-and-domain-modeling.mdc`). If a service function exceeds ~30 lines of
  real logic, check whether part belongs in `packages/domain`.

## Quick check before committing a file

- [ ] Does this file do exactly one thing?
- [ ] Is anything here duplicated elsewhere (extract it)?
- [ ] Is reusable UI/logic in the right shared home, not trapped in a route?
- [ ] Are cross-package imports through the barrel, not deep paths?
